From ccf13a0c667dd8a285c27977b346560762b27849 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 374/488] soh: name the 33 address-named symbols defined in
 z_bg_bdan_switch.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 33 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Bg_Bdan_Switch/z_bg_bdan_switch.c.

  * func_8086D0EC -> BgBdanSwitch_UpdateShape
    deduced, confidence HIGH: advances the wobble phase and derives the
    switch's draw radius, height and yOffset from it and the current press
    amount

  * func_8086D4B4 -> BgBdanSwitch_SetSwitchFlag
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sets this switch's flag once and plays the
    chest or chime attention sound

  * func_8086D548 -> BgBdanSwitch_ClearSwitchFlag
    deduced, confidence HIGH: clears this switch's flag, playing the chest
    sound for the YELLOW_TALL_2 type

  * func_8086D5C4 -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the unpressed idle and restores the
    full press amount

  * func_8086D5E0 -> BgBdanSwitch_Idle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits for the blue switch to be weighed down
    or for the player to stand on the yellow one

  * func_8086D67C -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupPress
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the pressing action and arms the
    100-frame camera wait

  * func_8086D694 -> BgBdanSwitch_Press
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sinks the switch by 0.2 a frame once the
    camera looks at it or the wait expires, then locks it down with a rumble

  * func_8086D730 -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupPressed
    deduced, confidence HIGH: snaps the switch fully down and installs the
    pressed action with a six-frame debounce

  * func_8086D754 -> BgBdanSwitch_Pressed
    deduced, confidence HIGH: releases the blue switch once nothing weighs
    it down, or the yellow one once its flag is cleared elsewhere

  * func_8086D7FC -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupRelease
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the rising action

  * func_8086D80C -> BgBdanSwitch_Release
    deduced, confidence HIGH: raises the switch by 0.2 a frame back to the
    idle

  * func_8086D86C -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupHeavyIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the YELLOW_HEAVY idle: installs the waiting
    action at full height

  * func_8086D888 -> BgBdanSwitch_HeavyIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits for the player to stand on the heavy
    switch

  * func_8086D8BC -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupHeavyHalfPress
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the half-press action

  * func_8086D8CC -> BgBdanSwitch_HeavyHalfPress
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sinks the heavy switch to 0.6 under the
    player's weight alone, with a rumble

  * func_8086D944 -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupHeavyFullPress
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the full-press action and arms the
    100-frame camera wait

  * func_8086D95C -> BgBdanSwitch_HeavyFullPress
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sinks the heavy switch the rest of the way
    once the camera looks at it or the wait expires

  * func_8086D9F8 -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupHeavyHalfPressed
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds the switch at 0.6 and installs the
    action that watches what the player is carrying

  * func_8086DA1C -> BgBdanSwitch_HeavyHalfPressed
    deduced, confidence HIGH: drives the switch fully down only while the
    player stands on it carrying Ruto, and lets it rise otherwise

  * func_8086DAB4 -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupHeavyRelease
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the heavy switch's rising action

  * func_8086DAC4 -> BgBdanSwitch_HeavyRelease
    deduced, confidence HIGH: raises the heavy switch back to its idle
    height

  * func_8086DB24 -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupHeavyDone
    deduced, confidence HIGH: locks the heavy switch fully down and installs
    the empty action

  * func_8086DB40 -> BgBdanSwitch_HeavyDone
    deduced, confidence HIGH: empty action: the heavy switch stays down for
    good

  * func_8086DB4C -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupTallIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the tall switch idle: installs the waiting
    action at double height

  * func_8086DB68 -> BgBdanSwitch_TallIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits for the tall switch to be hit, debounced
    by ten frames

  * func_8086DC30 -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupTallPress
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the tall switch's sinking action and
    arms the camera wait

  * func_8086DC48 -> BgBdanSwitch_TallPress
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sinks the tall switch by 0.3 a frame down to
    single height

  * func_8086DCCC -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupTallPressed
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds the tall switch at single height and
    installs its pressed action

  * func_8086DCE8 -> BgBdanSwitch_TallPressed
    deduced, confidence HIGH: releases the YELLOW_TALL_1 switch when its
    flag is cleared, and the YELLOW_TALL_2 one when it is hit again

  * func_8086DDA8 -> BgBdanSwitch_SetupTallRelease
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the tall switch's rising action and
